{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for notes/2026-10-01-research-jj.md, primary e51dc84dcdcac9be907dc6dfa8f22719f60bf9d7 at exact b3050dc6959f3c10d5eb550b28492d40ab81f435, under 966aeaad/bfb563fe and queued review a9c34999. I read all 12,816 bytes / 247 content lines, SHA256 8563588cd23c7047eb3572bd61b78b432b87eef85141e467cb08d63b72aa516f. The comparison and borrow/not-borrow direction are useful; a bounded dated correction is needed.\n\n1. P2 — Scope optimistic concurrency to the operation-log layer (lines 35–37,57,79,96–111,214–215). “Commands never wait” and blanket concurrency-without-locks overstate the mechanism. jj accepts divergent operation-store updates and later merges their views, but working-copy mutation has a lock and its pinned concurrency document warns that the Git backend is not entirely lock-free. State optimistic operation-log reconciliation separately from working-copy/backend synchronization, including ordinary I/O failure limits. The proposed plan sentence must retain that qualification. This does not diminish the useful contrast with Artroom's sequenced admission; it prevents that contrast from becoming a promise that multiple agents can safely mutate one working copy without coordination. [jj v0.45.1 concurrency](https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/blob/v0.45.1/docs/technical/concurrency.md), [working-copy contract](https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/blob/v0.45.1/lib/src/working_copy.rs).\n\n2. P2 — Distinguish an unresolved landing merge from jj conflict data in a Git tree (lines 65–69,124–137,165–173,226–229). Current R-LAND-4 fails the operation when its integration merge has a Git conflict. A jj conflict can instead be encoded in ordinary Git objects: the root conflict directories retain trees, and jj:trees carries the authoritative jj representation. Normal Git tools do not interpret that meaning, but Git storage does not itself guarantee its exclusion. jj's allow-conflicts push option reinforces the distinction. [Pinned format mapping](https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/blob/v0.45.1/docs/git-compatibility.md#format-mapping-details), [pinned changelog](https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/blob/v0.45.1/CHANGELOG.md). State clean resolved content as Artroom's intended policy outcome and the adopted client's still-owed explicit rule/witness, rather than an automatic consequence of main being a Git tree. Keep “probably outside-claim/fail checks” untested; no reproduction or implemented exclusion is asserted. This clarifies item 1 without pursuing item 3's live conflicted preparation.\n\n3. P3 — Preserve exact source identity and qualify interoperability/header evidence (lines 14–17,23–32,155–180,222–247). Pin the moving main links to jj v0.45.1 and pin the Artroom snapshot used for each source claim; retain retrieval dates and Source/Judgement/Untested distinctions. The pinned changelog supports the named feature dates, but a baseline version is not timeless “latest” status. Keep accepting jj clients as an adopted worth-doing direction, not demonstrated current support. Define the header witness: unchanged pushed/pinned commit objects and their reachability after landing differ from the newly built integration merge commit carrying that header. Metadata survives only where the actual pipeline preserves it; do not infer a copied change identity on a new merge object. No test is commissioned or run by this review.\n\n4. P3 — Reconcile the follow-up boundaries with the current application/workspace model (lines 71–82,174–180,193–204,222–231). Lane/generation is the code-review profile's useful analogue, not an assertion that every declared application uses the same change lifecycle. Current declared kinds and their signed bindings remain authoritative. Preserve header/change identity as author-supplied display/grouping metadata; it cannot identify the signer, certify equivalence, qualify a verdict or carry evidence. N1's proposal/interdiff work and C2's durable workspace/checkpoint work are related owners, not proof that jj support or per-change history is complete. Future header/client/rule work and original source-note integration must remain distinct from planning adoption and any actual new commissioning. Append-only undo is a good analogy for undo adding a new operation; do not turn that into an Artroom-style guarantee that all local operation history is permanently retained.\n\nPreserve the recorded choices: items 1 and 2 are worth doing; item 3 is not pursued; item 4 remains undecided. No comparison correction cuts their scope or adds a first-Jam gate. The proposed section 3 sentence can keep jj's local Git-backed change identity, operation views, undo and stored conflicts, with qualified optimistic concurrency and conditional client interoperability.\n\nThe rest of the full comparison is supported at this planning level: jj's local version-control/history-editing role versus a shared signed sequencer; stable change IDs versus rewritten commit IDs; snapshots/evolution/operation views; undo as a new operation; stored conflict simplification; multiple workspaces; and distinct admission, review, policy, attention and membership responsibilities. This is a comparison of native responsibilities, not a claim that jj cannot participate in external review systems.\n\nArchitecture: borrow local-client interoperability and useful per-change presentation while preserving one ordered Room admission/publication model. Security: verified signatures, current roles/delegations, exact bindings and recorded review/check predicates govern authority; author-supplied headers and local operation metadata do not. Simplification: leave local history editing and conflicts in the user's client, and retain the existing clean-content admission/landing policies rather than adding the rejected live-conflict mechanism.\n\nValidation was read-only: complete exact note/provenance, targeted R-LAND-4 at main e6e67828, pinned jj v0.45.1 concurrency/working-copy/Git-compatibility/conflict/operation documentation and changelog, plus an independent full-note primary-source check. No jj installation/command, application suite, repeated gate, provider/credential operation, source edit, implementation commissioning or source landing occurred.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e51dc84dcdcac9be907dc6dfa8f22719f60bf9d7","binding":"assigned","head":"b3050dc6959f3c10d5eb550b28492d40ab81f435","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6c5530c3b32731d4a73dd41a10f81e48c1c27b99\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bfb563fe704b11ac19a48b9c0a924376bec05dc7\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:25bede37003ee7b7b82e745129a84f5d40bd8873","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}